  {
   "key": "0x10",
   "name": "reset ext status",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
     "lines": "10636-10640"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
     "lines": "10652"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
     "function": "z80sio_channel::do_sioreg_wr0",
     "case": [
      "WR0_RESET_EXT_STATUS"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
     "function": "z80sio_channel::reset_ext_status"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Command 2 is Reset External/Status Interrupts.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10636",
       "sha": "4be1e4c60103cb4b5de19c1016991d2a43824c34ea5c9ff4ceaada3a90dcc7d0"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The Reset External/Status Interrupts command, listed on the row 2 0 1 0, re-enables the latched RR0 status bits, again allowing Interrupts to occur.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10638-10639",
       "sha": "0c395f750c7d284cd7386bea36e097e7f4063926d1a37097afad957cfcd995bd"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10652",
       "sha": "77e5e1fbc430c044b7caa7e607618af802389b7ece5dcfe5f60084ce790799a4"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "After an External/Status interrupt, such as a change on a modem line or a break condition, the status bits of RR0 are latched.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10636-10638",
       "sha": "33bd6cbd917bacf79b9eb1abf183a65e343d73ae9b175d9c24332058734d5641"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Latching the status bits captures short pulses until the CPU has time to read the change.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10639-10640",
       "sha": "1b09044b4f2e900a651a237624f0f5b47c9c8ee19251593f16986bbf8d72dc51"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "text": "The command also copies the current CTS and DCD input pins into RR0, and the sync input too unless WR4 selects a synchronous mode.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
       "lines": "1383",
       "sha": "a075dcbcff162b944957c0f5785d1b9ddbd6fdb102124d27d69c5ed0875aaf41"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
       "lines": "1396-1405",
       "sha": "17b1d49af01242cf15fbde71f37cb1b48e5bbdc1a03bb8a6bc4106c0ab95ee36"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
       "lines": "1408-1414",
       "sha": "ae11d0de9013775939d8144996b16a300626bde6fb25e548e8d4f6fba7f9d1a7"
      }
     ],
     "vs": "extra"
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
