  {
   "key": "0x18",
   "name": "channel reset",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
     "lines": "10641-10647"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
     "lines": "10653"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
     "function": "z80sio_channel::do_sioreg_wr0",
     "case": [
      "WR0_CHANNEL_RESET"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
     "lines": "1153-1154"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
     "function": "z80sio_device::reset_interrupts"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Command 3 is Channel Reset.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10641",
       "sha": "3d5a7db5df83b602ddb59277d38d97f9ee5d724c02a0af3c3226ccdcf0b0cefa"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The Channel Reset command, listed on the row 3 0 1 1, performs the same function as an External Reset, but on a single channel.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10641-10642",
       "sha": "43c1fdb60a8b83afc559cdc7cf8624ab29e5192ad9b4bd5d161ae5677cbb1095"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10653",
       "sha": "d1feef883609d1d5d368e80122f4ca6a2e0e68f51106e9c0478964e50c12138d"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A Channel A Reset also resets the interrupt prioritization logic.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10642-10643",
       "sha": "50503a632b17a19093a4e7541544a935b483c98620b911f692bb3b479516ad1f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "All control registers for the channel must be rewritten after a Channel Reset command.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10643-10644",
       "sha": "b4987ec395e7c9114f70c19fab56409b78c8941e633e2b7f50ec1e3ce883ab66"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "After a Z80 SIO Channel Reset, add four system clock cycles before more commands or controls write to that channel, normally one Op Code fetch.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:UM0081.raw.txt",
       "lines": "10645-10647",
       "sha": "fd3551cf7b6892c93f4378fefb8a10840e1af65878885a1e6d2d43cdf74fb295"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "text": "On a Channel A reset MAME zeroes the interrupt state word of every interrupt source, prioritization state included; a FIXME there asks whether it should reset them all.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
       "lines": "1152-1154",
       "sha": "b2de6b5fc619c4a839b558817277260222e419ef0c18aba64e37c50ab845a243"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
       "lines": "670-673",
       "sha": "804418c30a27c74911eed659652120b1a976f0adc21b5b722badeb6a7c6a995b"
      }
     ],
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "3"
    },
    {
     "n": "7",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "text": "On an MK68564 channel MAME's reset also clears the transmit auto-enable flag and the baud rate generator's time constant, control and state, and stops its timer.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/machine/z80sio.cpp",
       "lines": "1157-1165",
       "sha": "68caeee4e3d14b1a7650b0d6cdeb974b6c86f2389d64fe293592502a626f1dbd"
      }
     ],
     "vs": "extra"
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
